                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "here's a short rifter review, from the fact I've played it for ... probably an hour.\n-precision platformer where momentum matters. The gameplay is super fun.\n- There is a bug where you need to patch the game yourself for it to be fixed [you have to unpack the jar file that you get when the game downloads, change the last line of the postProcess.vert shader to (0,0, 1,1) instead of a self-referential pointer, then repack it from inside the folder). Without this bug fixed you are invisible at the beginning of the game, when dashing, and when taking damage, which makes the game way harder and much less fun in my opinion. The bug has existed in the game for I think six years at this point so I ... doubt it will be fixed?\n\nAssuming you can fix the bug yourself, it's super fun and completely worth it. Given that the bug exists I would probably only purchase this on sale, and knowing that you'll have to do that.",
